INT. DELIVERY WAREHOUSE - LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

The warehouse is very big and very cold. Yellow lamps hum over rows of brown boxes. Outside, snow falls on the empty parking lot.

ADRIAN, 40s, stands next to a pallet. He holds a small black phone. A forklift is silent behind him.

A side door SLAMS. KESTREL, 30s, walks in. They wear a gray coat and carry no bag.

                    ADRIAN
You are late. I said eleven.

                    KESTREL
Traffic was bad. Also, I do not like this place.

He looks at them for a long time. His hand moves to the pallet, slowly.

                    ADRIAN
Where is the package?

                    KESTREL
It is safe. First you tell me who sold my name.

The phone BUZZES in his hand. He does not look at it. Above them, the cold wind makes the roof metal sing.

                    ADRIAN
Nobody sold. You make a story in your head.

                    KESTREL
They told me you would say this.

This is the last time they will trust anyone in this city.

He takes one step forward. She, no, they, do not move. A truck engine RUMBLES far away.

                    ADRIAN
Give me the package. Please.

                    KESTREL
Give me the name.

He opens his coat. A metal box CLICKS on the floor between them.
